    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13593" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπορραίω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bereave</i> one <i>of</i> a thing, c. dupl. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅστις σ᾽ ἀέκοντα βίηφι κτήματ᾽
					ἀπορραίσεἰ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					1.404
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπορραῖσαι [αὐτὸν] φίλον ἦτορ</span>
			<i>bereave</i> him <i>of</i> life, <i><span class="en">
				16.428
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυμὸν ἀπορραῖσαι</span> (sc.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνδρας</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Emp.
				128
			</span></i>: c. gen. rei, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή τιν᾽ ἀπορραίσειν γεράων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					393
				</span></i>
			.</div>
